WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:04.837
♪ <i>It seems today that all you see</i> ♪

00:04.838 --> 00:08.174
♪ <i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i> ♪

00:08.175 --> 00:11.511
♪ <i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i> ♪

00:11.512 --> 00:14.847
♪ <i>On which we used to rely?</i> ♪

00:14.848 --> 00:18.226
♪ <i>Lucky there's a family guy</i> ♪

00:18.227 --> 00:21.604
♪ <i>Lucky there's a man who
positively can do</i> ♪

00:21.605 --> 00:23.189
♪ <i>All the things that make us</i> ♪

00:23.190 --> 00:24.899
♪ <i>Laugh and cry</i> ♪

00:24.900 --> 00:30.155
♪ <i>He's... a... fam... ily... guy!</i> ♪

00:39.540 --> 00:41.374
I won a chain saw.

00:41.375 --> 00:43.668
What? What are you talking about?

00:43.669 --> 00:45.294
Some lady up the block is giving away

00:45.295 --> 00:47.380
all of her husband's stuff
'cause he shot himself

00:47.381 --> 00:49.006
- in the face.
- Oh, my god!

00:49.007 --> 00:51.175
I've seen that lady.
He did the right thing.

00:51.176 --> 00:53.010
That's also how we got this couch.

00:53.011 --> 00:54.554
Basically everything in this house

00:54.555 --> 00:56.722
is Christmas suicide furniture.

00:56.723 --> 00:58.891
Donna, they had a bullhorn.

00:58.892 --> 01:01.727
I don't know why,
but they had a bullhorn.

01:01.728 --> 01:03.771
Cleveland, it's time for lunch.

01:03.772 --> 01:05.773
What do I want? Sammich!

01:05.774 --> 01:07.733
When do I want it? Now!

01:07.734 --> 01:10.946
♪ <i>I ain't eatin' no lipton soup.</i> ♪

01:15.576 --> 01:19.078
So, kids, bonnie just told me
about the neatest thing.

01:19.079 --> 01:20.871
It's called a podcast.

01:20.872 --> 01:23.874
I guess it's like a-a radio show
on your phone.

01:23.875 --> 01:26.085
Have you heard of these? Podcasts.

01:26.086 --> 01:28.379
Yeah, Mom, we know what podcasts are.

01:28.380 --> 01:29.797
Huh.

01:29.798 --> 01:33.050
I guess these types of things
take a while to reach the moms.

01:33.051 --> 01:35.262
I'll have to let Bonnie know.

01:48.567 --> 01:50.776
Wow, really?

01:50.777 --> 01:52.778
Mom, Stewie needs his sausage cut

01:52.779 --> 01:54.238
and his butter spread.

01:54.239 --> 01:56.157
Here, let me get that for you, buddy.

02:07.961 --> 02:10.713
There you go. Eat up, little guy.

02:10.714 --> 02:13.466
Damn it, Peter.
You ruined Stewie's chair.

02:15.218 --> 02:17.971
And Bonnie wants to know
what all the noise is.

02:22.434 --> 02:24.518
- Amazing.
- Ooh.

02:24.519 --> 02:26.646
- Wow, it's Willem Dafoe!
- That's right.

02:26.647 --> 02:29.106
Since Willem Dafoe
has more bones in his face

02:29.107 --> 02:30.983
than most people have
in their entire body,

02:30.984 --> 02:33.569
he's perfect for carving,
'cause the angles are so sharp.

02:33.570 --> 02:34.695
It's beautiful, Peter.

02:34.696 --> 02:36.572
Yeah, I just love William Dafoe.

02:36.573 --> 02:38.324
It's not "William," it's "Willem."

02:38.325 --> 02:39.825
Yeah, that's what I said. "William."

02:39.826 --> 02:41.661
He was in<i> Spider-Man</i> with Kristin Dunst.

02:41.662 --> 02:44.080
<i>- Kirsten</i> Dunst.
- Right. Kirsten Dunce.

02:44.081 --> 02:46.916
- It's not "Dunce," it's "Dunst."
- Yeah, Kristin Dunce.

02:46.917 --> 02:49.168
In the movie,
she dated William Dafoe's son.

02:49.169 --> 02:52.296
Spell it, Joe! Spell
what you are saying right now.

02:52.297 --> 02:53.547
Well, I'll give it a shot.

02:53.548 --> 02:57.761
K-Y-R-H...

02:59.096 --> 03:01.681
Look, there's a reason I became
a cop and not a spellman.

03:01.682 --> 03:03.516
- A what?
- A spellman.

03:03.517 --> 03:05.685
- "Spellman" is not a thing, Joe!
- Sure it is.

03:05.686 --> 03:07.937
Fireman, longshoreman, spellman.

03:07.938 --> 03:09.689
Stop me when I'm wrong.

03:09.690 --> 03:11.941
- He's getting too many right.
- Now I'm starting to think

03:11.942 --> 03:13.401
there<i> is</i> such a thing as a spellman.

03:13.402 --> 03:14.652
Hey, guys. Check it out.

03:14.653 --> 03:16.570
- It's groot.
- Oh, yeah.

03:16.571 --> 03:19.533
From that Marble movie.

03:23.662 --> 03:25.037
What are you doing?!

03:25.038 --> 03:28.082
- Turn that chain saw off!
- Not a chance, Lois.

03:28.083 --> 03:30.167
You know how hard it was
to get that thing started?

03:30.168 --> 03:33.839
It was even worse than trying to
cover anything with saran wrap.

04:35.650 --> 04:37.569
Oh.

05:20.570 --> 05:22.238
Perfect.

05:22.239 --> 05:24.907
Can't wait to throw that out
in two weeks.

05:34.459 --> 05:37.211
Peter! What's going on out here?!

05:37.212 --> 05:39.505
Oh, hey, Lois.
I'm just hollowing out this tree

05:39.506 --> 05:41.006
for the Keebler elves to live in.

05:41.007 --> 05:42.716
- Awesome!
- I know, right?

05:42.717 --> 05:44.385
Gonna get us a lifetime supply

05:44.386 --> 05:47.596
of fresh-baked-but-still-stale
supermarket cookies.

05:47.597 --> 05:50.475
All right,
time for a little elfin magic.

05:57.399 --> 06:00.568
Ow! Oh! My arm! Oh, son of a bitch!

06:10.245 --> 06:12.413
- Oh, my god!
- Mom, look.

06:15.792 --> 06:18.919
Aw. Poor thing
must've been living in the tree.

06:20.630 --> 06:23.340
- And its foot seems hurt.
- It's even worse than that.

06:23.341 --> 06:26.302
It looks like the tree landed
on its parents and killed them.

06:26.303 --> 06:28.095
Nobody touch
the smooshed squirrel bodies!

06:28.096 --> 06:30.848
Ooh, I got to get my camera.

06:30.849 --> 06:33.475
That girl is one giant red flag.

06:33.476 --> 06:35.854
Stewie, this squirrel needs help.

06:37.397 --> 06:40.441
I wonder if...
M-maybe I could take care of it.

06:40.442 --> 06:42.359
I don't know if you should do it
on your own.

06:42.360 --> 06:44.862
Could be a lot of work.

06:44.863 --> 06:47.156
Would... Would you do it with me?

06:47.157 --> 06:48.908
Well, I-I don't think it...

06:55.540 --> 06:58.334
You know what? I think
that's a marvelous idea, Chris.

06:58.335 --> 07:01.045
I daresay we would make
outstanding parents

07:01.046 --> 07:03.797
- to this squirrel.
- Hey there, Griffin boys.

07:03.798 --> 07:06.634
I saw this tree go down. Any loot in it?

07:06.635 --> 07:08.677
Elven treasures?

07:08.678 --> 07:10.679
Uh, no.

07:10.680 --> 07:13.349
Hey, donna, the tree's just regular.

07:13.350 --> 07:16.061
Go to work, Cleveland!

07:22.025 --> 07:24.109
Well, somebody's getting big and strong.

07:24.110 --> 07:25.861
Did you hear that one vet technician

07:25.862 --> 07:27.488
say our little squirrel here

07:27.489 --> 07:30.699
was in the 70th percentile
for height and weight?

07:30.700 --> 07:32.701
No. Which vet tech said that?

07:32.702 --> 07:34.203
The one with the neck tattoo.

07:34.204 --> 07:36.497
- Which one with the neck tattoo?
- The one we saw

07:36.498 --> 07:38.499
smoking in the parking lot
when we were leaving.

07:38.500 --> 07:40.626
Again, you're gonna
have to be more specific.

07:40.627 --> 07:42.836
The one wearing pajama bottoms as pants.

07:42.837 --> 07:45.130
- Sorry, I don't...
- The girl one!

07:45.131 --> 07:48.050
Oh, yeah, with the half-shaved
head. She was nice.

07:48.051 --> 07:50.178
Well, I'll bet this cutie is hungry.

07:53.598 --> 07:55.307
Wh-what are you doing?

07:55.308 --> 07:57.101
Don't film me. Film the baby.

07:57.102 --> 07:59.061
But you're both so cute.

07:59.062 --> 08:01.188
This role, it-it suits you.

08:01.189 --> 08:03.148
It's like you've been waiting
your whole life

08:03.149 --> 08:04.483
to be this person.

08:04.484 --> 08:06.276
Shush, you're going to make me cry.

08:06.277 --> 08:08.737
Aw! He made a little toot.

08:08.738 --> 08:12.492
That was me. It was
one of my cross-legged ones.

08:13.576 --> 08:16.204
I should probably stop recording.

08:20.625 --> 08:23.127
Well, if it's your elbow
that's bothering you,

08:23.128 --> 08:25.087
we should start
by checking your reflexes.

08:26.715 --> 08:28.257
- Okay, they seem all right.
- Oh, that's good.

08:28.258 --> 08:30.217
But you got to help me.
My arm really hurts.

08:30.218 --> 08:32.636
It all started after I got a chain saw.

08:32.637 --> 08:33.971
Hmm, is that right?

08:33.972 --> 08:36.557
Well, it sounds to me like
you may have chain saw elbow.

08:36.558 --> 08:39.560
- "Chain saw elbow"?
- Yes, it's all explained

08:39.561 --> 08:40.728
in this video.

08:40.729 --> 08:42.187
<i>Hi, I'm Tommy Lee Jones.</i>

08:42.188 --> 08:43.939
<i>Congratulations on suffering</i>

08:43.940 --> 08:46.316
<i>from the coolest arm ailment there is:</i>

08:46.317 --> 08:48.068
<i>Chain saw elbow.</i>

08:48.069 --> 08:50.696
<i>As a celebrity dick,
it's always been my passion</i>

08:50.697 --> 08:52.614
<i>to own a ranch in a low-tax state</i>

08:52.615 --> 08:54.575
<i>that I list as my primary residence.</i>

08:54.576 --> 08:57.036
<i>And when I'm not pouting
at awards shows,</i>

08:57.037 --> 08:58.620
<i>I'm out in the field cutting firewood</i>

08:58.621 --> 09:00.956
<i>for a staged Instagram post.</i>

09:00.957 --> 09:04.209
<i>Sometimes I overdo it,
end up with chain saw elbow.</i>

09:04.210 --> 09:06.628
<i>Now here's fellow ranch owner
Dennis Quaid</i>

09:06.629 --> 09:09.089
<i>to discuss the dangers of tractor ass.</i>

09:09.090 --> 09:11.717
<i>So, you have tractor ass.</i>

09:11.718 --> 09:14.386
Okay, so how much
synthetic opioid do you need?

09:14.387 --> 09:16.930
I'm trying to prescribe enough
to earn a fanny pack.

09:16.931 --> 09:18.557
A-aren't there any other options?

09:18.558 --> 09:20.684
Well, there's a trucker hat,
but those look stupid on me.

09:20.685 --> 09:23.562
You know, sometimes joint pain
is connected to back issues.

09:23.563 --> 09:25.856
Have you ever had
a chiropractic adjustment?

09:25.857 --> 09:27.357
- What's that?
- It's a procedure

09:27.358 --> 09:29.318
where a guy who couldn't
get into medical school

09:29.319 --> 09:31.361
- tries to rip your head off.
- Does it work?

09:31.362 --> 09:32.696
If you believe it works.

09:32.697 --> 09:34.281
It's kind of like the polar express.

09:34.282 --> 09:36.575
- Let's do it!
- Okay, I'll give it a shot.

09:36.576 --> 09:38.952
But this type of thing
is usually done in strip malls

09:38.953 --> 09:41.289
next to a little caesars.

09:53.134 --> 09:54.718
Holy crap! What happened?

09:54.719 --> 09:57.137
Well, I think we simply found
your true height.

09:57.138 --> 09:59.473
Before years of poor posture
and wear and tear

09:59.474 --> 10:02.184
- crushed your spirit and your spine.
- Wow.

10:02.185 --> 10:04.436
Mr. Griffin, let's discuss risk factors.

10:04.437 --> 10:06.897
Do you lead a lifestyle
that's sedentary?

10:06.898 --> 10:08.315
<i>Pet sedentary?</i>

10:08.316 --> 10:10.067
I'm saying you need
to strengthen your core

10:10.068 --> 10:11.443
and exercise regularly.

10:11.444 --> 10:14.489
- Is that the hat?
- Stupid, right?

10:17.617 --> 10:19.701
I know the holidays
are still months away,

10:19.702 --> 10:20.994
but I was just so excited

10:20.995 --> 10:23.163
to take our family Christmas card photo.

10:23.164 --> 10:26.667
Are you kidding? I love it.

10:26.668 --> 10:28.043
You know what, Chris?

10:28.044 --> 10:30.796
I feel like I'm ready to start trying...

10:30.797 --> 10:33.632
To find another squirrel.

10:33.633 --> 10:34.758
What?

10:34.759 --> 10:37.052
Nothing. I just...

10:37.053 --> 10:39.847
I just hit the lottery when I met you.

10:39.848 --> 10:41.348
Here's your photo.

10:41.349 --> 10:42.641
It's the only one where the squirrel

10:42.642 --> 10:44.017
wasn't trying to bite your hand.

10:44.018 --> 10:46.019
- Ooh!
- Oh, I love it!

10:46.020 --> 10:48.313
- How much do we owe you?
- It's fine. Just keep it.

10:48.314 --> 10:50.358
Sears just closed forever.

10:55.363 --> 10:57.114
Whoa! Peter, what happened?

10:57.115 --> 10:59.074
Did you tease that witch again?

10:59.075 --> 11:00.492
No, I got a back adjustment.

11:00.493 --> 11:02.286
Turns out I've been this tall all along.

11:02.287 --> 11:04.413
- You don't say.
- Well, that's amazing.

11:04.414 --> 11:06.373
Why are you still wearing
the same pants?

11:06.374 --> 11:08.750
I don't know. I only get
pants at Christmas, so...

11:08.751 --> 11:10.544
I'll get pants at Christmas.

11:10.545 --> 11:13.297
- So, how is it being that tall?
- It's okay, I guess.

11:13.298 --> 11:16.049
Although I've noticed I'm a lot
more clumsy in the bedroom.

11:19.012 --> 11:20.345
I'm so sorry.

11:20.346 --> 11:22.557
You two keep going.
I'm gonna clean this up.

11:27.145 --> 11:30.105
Stewie! Stewie, come quick!

11:30.106 --> 11:32.107
its first steps?

11:32.108 --> 11:33.692
We've got to film this!

11:33.693 --> 11:35.277
I know, I know!

11:39.449 --> 11:40.949
Look at that!

11:40.950 --> 11:42.784
Oh, I'm going to cry!

11:42.785 --> 11:44.786
I've never felt this proud.

11:44.787 --> 11:47.206
That's going on Instagram right now.

11:47.207 --> 11:49.374
Totally! But we should
pair it with a song

11:49.375 --> 11:51.251
about steps or walking.

11:51.252 --> 11:53.879
Oh, my god, yes. "Walking on Sunshine."

11:53.880 --> 11:55.297
Oh, that would sell it.

11:55.298 --> 11:57.382
Sell what? That we're totally cliché?

11:57.383 --> 12:00.260
- How about "Step by Step"?
- New Kids on the Block?

12:00.261 --> 12:02.095
No. The Eddie Rabbitt version.

12:02.096 --> 12:03.805
And have people think we're 100?

12:03.806 --> 12:05.057
Let's do "Walking in Memphis."

12:05.058 --> 12:06.808
I will concede that's a good song,

12:06.809 --> 12:09.603
but we don't live in Memphis,
so I find it confusing.

12:09.604 --> 12:11.230
What about "Walk Like an Egyptian"?

12:11.231 --> 12:13.023
Well, we don't live in Egypt either.

12:13.024 --> 12:15.400
Ah. Hoisted on my own petard.

12:15.401 --> 12:17.069
"Nobody Walks in L.A."

12:17.070 --> 12:18.528
Again, we do not live in L.A.

12:18.529 --> 12:21.448
Ooh, let's do "I Love L.A."!

12:21.449 --> 12:22.866
Do you know what?

12:22.867 --> 12:24.201
This is going to surprise you, Chris,

12:24.202 --> 12:25.244
but I agree with you.

12:25.245 --> 12:27.497
Let's use "I Love L.A."

12:28.122 --> 12:30.958
♪ <i>I love L.A.</i> ♪

12:30.959 --> 12:33.293
- It's perfect!
- ♪<i> We love it!</i> ♪

12:33.294 --> 12:35.671
Yes, this will really tell people that

12:35.672 --> 12:37.715
♪<i> I love L.A.</i> ♪

12:39.467 --> 12:41.302
♪ <i>We love it!</i> ♪

12:42.262 --> 12:45.223
♪ <i>I love L.A.</i> ♪

12:51.229 --> 12:53.647
Thank you all for coming today.

12:53.648 --> 12:57.109
It means a lot to Stewie and me
that you would be here.

12:57.110 --> 12:58.277
I got this, Chris.

12:58.278 --> 12:59.945
Everyone, after the service,

12:59.946 --> 13:01.822
you are all invited to a small reception

13:01.823 --> 13:03.740
to honor our beloved squirrel.

13:03.741 --> 13:06.118
Nothing fancy.
Just acorns and puddle water.

13:06.119 --> 13:08.120
It'll take place
either on top of the fence

13:08.121 --> 13:09.454
or along a power line.

13:09.455 --> 13:10.956
But, first, please join me

13:10.957 --> 13:13.041
in a frozen-in-place moment of silence,

13:13.042 --> 13:16.004
followed by a manic scattering
in all directions.

13:27.640 --> 13:29.641
All right, the Quahog Fair.

13:29.642 --> 13:31.768
Hey, Peter,
would you get off your phone?

13:31.769 --> 13:33.895
Sorry, young girls
keep killing each other

13:33.896 --> 13:35.981
'cause they think
I'm the Slender Man now.

13:35.982 --> 13:37.524
Are-are you...

13:37.525 --> 13:39.026
Are you telling them to kill each other?

13:39.027 --> 13:40.361
It's just a goof.

13:43.531 --> 13:45.699
You sure you're not too tall for this?

13:45.700 --> 13:48.036
Nah, it's gonna be great.

13:51.664 --> 13:52.998
Yay!

13:52.999 --> 13:55.417
- Ow! Who kicked me?!
- Sorry!

13:55.418 --> 13:57.711
- What the hell?!
- My bad.

13:57.712 --> 14:00.380
- Ow! Who's doing that?
- It's that jerk up there!

14:01.966 --> 14:04.217
It's Slender Man!

14:04.218 --> 14:05.469
Kill yourselves!

14:05.470 --> 14:08.430
- Peter!
- Come on. It's just a goof.

14:19.817 --> 14:22.152
Don't you dare touch its bedroom!

14:22.153 --> 14:23.945
The squirrel is gone, Stewie,

14:23.946 --> 14:26.656
and there's nothing we can do
to change that.

14:26.657 --> 14:28.533
Yes, thanks to you.
If it weren't for you,

14:28.534 --> 14:30.535
our sweet baby would still be alive.

14:30.536 --> 14:32.412
- Me?
- That's right.

14:32.413 --> 14:33.830
If you hadn't kept the squirrel
up so late,

14:33.831 --> 14:35.374
none of this would have happened.

14:35.375 --> 14:37.667
That squirrel
should have been in bed, Chris.

14:37.668 --> 14:39.753
It was 7:45!

14:39.754 --> 14:41.671
What? I'm not the one

14:41.672 --> 14:44.966
who just had to post the video
to Instagram that very second.

14:44.967 --> 14:47.803
You couldn't even enjoy
the moment for one damn minute

14:47.804 --> 14:50.472
before desperately groveling
for online approval

14:50.473 --> 14:51.890
from aunts you never talk to

14:51.891 --> 14:54.559
and past coworkers you don't even like!

14:54.560 --> 14:56.520
Is that so?
Well, if you had a newer phone,

14:56.521 --> 14:58.855
it wouldn't have taken so long
to upload the video.

14:58.856 --> 15:02.526
Well,<i> excuse</i> me
for not having a fancier phone.

15:02.527 --> 15:04.403
I'm only a paperboy!

15:04.404 --> 15:07.615
Oh, I'm well aware
that you're only a paperboy.

15:12.120 --> 15:14.496
Ah, perfect. I see you're using again.

15:14.497 --> 15:16.498
Oh, I wonder why.

15:16.499 --> 15:18.750
And don't think I didn't smell
the Charleston Chew

15:18.751 --> 15:20.127
on your breath at the service.

15:20.128 --> 15:21.920
Maybe if you'd been a little sharper

15:21.921 --> 15:23.505
on the evening in question,
we wouldn't be in this...

15:23.506 --> 15:25.632
I had four skittles that night!

15:25.633 --> 15:27.008
That's not zero!

15:27.009 --> 15:28.927
You knew there was a dog in the house.

15:28.928 --> 15:30.971
He's practically your best friend!

15:30.972 --> 15:33.223
Or maybe even more than that.

15:33.224 --> 15:35.767
You shut your damn mouth!

15:35.768 --> 15:37.394
Oh, this is awful.

15:37.395 --> 15:41.648
Why does death seem so much
easier in the<i> Rocky</i> movies?

15:41.649 --> 15:42.816
Goodbye, mick.

15:45.027 --> 15:47.863
Oh, wai... you're just gonna
put him in a drawer?

15:47.864 --> 15:50.657
- What are you, like, filing him?
- Yes, for tax reasons.

15:50.658 --> 15:51.658
Jews don't die.

15:51.659 --> 15:53.326
They just slowly depreciate

15:53.327 --> 15:56.079
and then are eventually written off.

16:00.460 --> 16:02.335
What's the matter, Peter?

16:02.336 --> 16:04.129
I'm just sick of being tall.

16:04.130 --> 16:07.382
I had a hard enough time getting
everything in the toilet before.

16:07.383 --> 16:09.009
I want my old body back.

16:09.010 --> 16:11.428
Well, there is a way.

16:11.429 --> 16:12.762
What is it?

16:12.763 --> 16:14.347
Lock the front door.

16:15.475 --> 16:17.601
Peter, if you really want
to get shorter,

16:17.602 --> 16:19.603
- I can berate you.
- What?

16:19.604 --> 16:21.897
The female power to belittle is such

16:21.898 --> 16:25.233
that the recipient can
physically shrink in stature.

16:25.234 --> 16:28.195
That's why husbands and wives
are the same height in old age.

16:28.196 --> 16:30.530
Lois, berate me.

16:30.531 --> 16:34.075
Okay, Peter, but if I do this,
I<i> really</i> got to do it.

16:34.076 --> 16:35.118
Do it.

16:39.790 --> 16:41.917
For starters, you're a failure.

16:41.918 --> 16:42.959
gah!

16:42.960 --> 16:44.169
You didn't go to college.

16:44.170 --> 16:45.670
Daddy pays our mortgage.

16:45.671 --> 16:47.506
And you're a terrible husband
and father.

16:47.507 --> 16:49.341
- Ouch!
- Your whole life

16:49.342 --> 16:51.301
is a pattern of hateable noises.

16:51.302 --> 16:53.386
- Ooh!
- The way you chew a banana

16:53.387 --> 16:55.138
makes it sound
like it's filled with bones.

16:55.139 --> 16:57.390
- Ouch!
- I loathe the little wheeze

16:57.391 --> 16:59.267
at the crest of every breath you take.

16:59.268 --> 17:02.020
- Yikes!
- I hate the one story you tell

17:02.021 --> 17:05.774
at every cocktail party
about almost meeting John Kerry.

17:05.775 --> 17:07.025
That's a good story.

17:07.026 --> 17:08.360
You didn't even meet him!

17:08.361 --> 17:09.778
Almost.

17:09.779 --> 17:13.406
Your eyeglass lenses
have been smudged for 19 years.

17:13.407 --> 17:14.824
Aw, crap.

17:14.825 --> 17:16.243
Everyone hates it when you see fireworks

17:16.244 --> 17:18.245
and you announce, "this is the finale!"

17:18.246 --> 17:20.664
- Please stop.
- Pink Floyd is multiple guys!

17:20.665 --> 17:21.748
He is?

17:21.749 --> 17:23.542
You're so predictable.

17:23.543 --> 17:25.460
I know every word that's gonna
come out of your mouth

17:25.461 --> 17:27.212
before you even say it.

17:27.213 --> 17:29.673
Balderdash. Heavens. Stop that.

17:29.674 --> 17:32.926
I worked for purolator courier
before they went bankrupt.

17:32.927 --> 17:34.427
Appearance.

17:34.428 --> 17:35.762
Intelligence.

17:35.763 --> 17:37.889
Penis size.

17:38.933 --> 17:40.977
And another thing...!

17:44.855 --> 17:47.525
Well, Lois, you are a master.

17:51.279 --> 17:53.196
Well, let me first start by saying

17:53.197 --> 17:55.907
y'all's doing
your relationship a huge favor

17:55.908 --> 17:57.867
by coming to couples counseling.

17:57.868 --> 18:00.870
Now, why don't y'all start
by each trying to suck up to me

18:00.871 --> 18:03.290
so I can choose who I'm-a side with?

18:03.291 --> 18:05.667
Well, I'm Stewart,
and I would love to offer you

18:05.668 --> 18:07.252
a freshly baked brownie.

18:07.253 --> 18:09.170
Mmm. Oh, my.

18:09.171 --> 18:11.881
Someone's already in the lead.

18:11.882 --> 18:14.926
I'm Chris. I'm somehow
both signing the checks

18:14.927 --> 18:16.136
and always wrong.

18:16.137 --> 18:18.013
See,<i> this</i> is why we came.

18:18.014 --> 18:19.723
Right? It's this all day.

18:19.724 --> 18:21.266
Oh, that's right.

18:21.267 --> 18:23.518
I'm not allowed to mention
I'm paying for this.

18:23.519 --> 18:25.395
It's both 100% true

18:25.396 --> 18:28.815
and also the worst thing
anybody could possibly say.

18:28.816 --> 18:31.443
He had his arms crossed
the whole ride here.

18:31.444 --> 18:33.278
Excuse me if I don't buy into

18:33.279 --> 18:35.864
this whole headshrinker business.

18:35.865 --> 18:38.033
Stewie promised
he'd make healthy meals for us,

18:38.034 --> 18:40.368
but all he ever makes is frozen pizza.

18:40.369 --> 18:42.912
You said you loved pizza,
especially when I make

18:42.913 --> 18:44.831
the ones with the crust
made of "hwheat."

18:44.832 --> 18:46.374
He also does<i> that.</i>

18:46.375 --> 18:48.043
Oh, really? Go ahead.

18:48.044 --> 18:50.295
Show him those girls
you follow on Instagram.

18:50.296 --> 18:52.714
It's all bosoms and derrieres on there.

18:52.715 --> 18:55.592
This is all stuff I've talked
about with my life coach, Kyle.

18:55.593 --> 18:57.344
Yeah, "life coach."

18:57.345 --> 18:59.596
Kyle's into you and you know it.

18:59.597 --> 19:01.139
What...?!

19:01.140 --> 19:04.225
Okay. Chris, why don't you tell
your side of the story

19:04.226 --> 19:06.269
while I share looks with Stewart
that say,

19:06.270 --> 19:08.980
"whoa, this is
what you got to deal with?"

19:08.981 --> 19:12.025
This is just so hard.

19:12.026 --> 19:14.486
Stewie won't stop blaming me
about the death,

19:14.487 --> 19:16.196
but it's not my fault.

19:16.197 --> 19:18.365
I didn't kill our squirrel.

19:18.366 --> 19:20.784
You know, I'm sad, too!

19:20.785 --> 19:23.119
I know. I-I just...

19:23.120 --> 19:25.997
I just don't know what to do
with all these feelings!

19:25.998 --> 19:30.210
Which is why... I suppose I've
been taking them out on you.

19:30.211 --> 19:32.087
I'm so sorry, Chris.

19:32.088 --> 19:34.214
Me, too, Stewie.

19:34.215 --> 19:36.049
We can't bring our baby back,

19:36.050 --> 19:39.761
but we'll always have Tuesday
through Friday of last week.

19:39.762 --> 19:41.179
Keep talking.

19:41.180 --> 19:42.597
I's just gonna open up this big book

19:42.598 --> 19:44.140
and use the time you're paying for

19:44.141 --> 19:46.685
to figure out
when you're next available.

19:46.686 --> 19:50.480
It was a true pleasure parenting
our squirrel with you, Chris.

19:50.481 --> 19:51.856
Likewise, Stewie.

19:51.857 --> 19:53.566
And although his life was brief,

19:53.567 --> 19:56.194
I'll always have
very fond memories of him.

19:56.195 --> 19:57.612
Wait, "him"?

19:57.613 --> 19:59.114
It-it was a her.

19:59.115 --> 20:00.782
No, it wasn't. The squirrel was a boy.

20:00.783 --> 20:02.659
What? That's crazy.

20:02.660 --> 20:05.203
- Chris, he was a boy.
- How do you know?

20:05.204 --> 20:07.038
Well, you've got to check
with your finger.

20:07.039 --> 20:09.708
But you really got to get it in there.

20:09.709 --> 20:12.335
Huh. Well, then maybe it's better

20:12.336 --> 20:15.673
that our baby you molested is dead.

20:22.054 --> 20:23.973
Ooh, fudge!

20:24.390 --> 20:26.266
"Don't be a grinch.

20:26.267 --> 20:29.185
Please return plate to G. Quagmire."

20:29.186 --> 20:31.814
Oh, great. So it's a gift and an errand.

20:44.952 --> 20:46.202
Oh.

20:46.203 --> 20:47.663
Oh, dear.

20:51.542 --> 20:54.670
♪ <i>I love L.A.</i> ♪

20:56.380 --> 20:58.006
♪ <i>We love it!</i> ♪

20:58.007 --> 21:00.968
All right! New pants!